course: dictionary
lesson: 2192
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cottage is a small house, usually in the countryside or a village, and it is often old and cosy. «Now she has a little cottage with sheep and has named every sheep after a relative.» The words little and sheep tell you that the cottage is small and out in the country.
explain: Clues in the words around a word help you choose its meaning. «Picture a holiday cottage in France at night» tells you that a cottage can be a place people stay for a holiday, not only a home where someone lives all year.
explain: Some words change meaning in different places. In Canada, going «to the cottage» in summer means going to a house by a lake. Read the whole sentence and look for clues such as the season or the place.
explain: Cottage is also part of longer names. Cottage cheese is a soft, lumpy cheese, and cottage pie is minced beef under mashed potato. In these words, cottage does not mean a house at all.
fact: Cottage means a small house, usually in the countryside or a village, and often old and cosy.
fact: In Canada, a cottage can be a holiday house by a lake or in the countryside.
fact: Cottage cheese is a soft white lumpy cheese.
fact: Cottage pie is minced beef topped with mashed potato.
fact: In stories, a cottage in the woods is often the home of a woodcutter or a grandmother.
exercise: «Now she has a little cottage with sheep.» What is a cottage? | Ship that sails on a lake | *A small house, often old and cosy, in the countryside | A type of sheep | A big office block in a city
exercise: In «Picture a holiday cottage in France at night», which word tells you the cottage is for a holiday? | night | *holiday | Picture | France
exercise: Cottage pie is a meal. What is in a cottage pie? | Fish and chips | *Minced beef topped with mashed potato | Cheese and jam pancakes | Soft lumpy cheese only
test: In Canada, a friend says, «We are going to the cottage this summer.» Where are they going? | To a tall building in a city | To a school in town | *To a house by a lake for the summer | To a farm for the winter
test: What is cottage cheese? | A hard, sharp cheese like cheddar | A drink made from fruit | *A soft white lumpy cheese | A bread roll
exam: Which best describes a cottage? | A boat for fishing on a lake | *A small, cosy house, often old, in the countryside or a village | A tall tower with a flag on top | A big office in the city
